# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gradle
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.gradle/
build/
.kotlin/

# The wrapper jar and properties MUST be committed. A clone without them cannot
# build — `./gradlew` is the bootstrap, not an artifact of it. These negations are
# defensive: a global gitignore or a stray `*.jar` rule would otherwise drop the jar
# silently, and the failure only shows up on someone else's machine.
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Java / JVM
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.class
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/
# Screenshots from the browser checks (frontend/e2e)
frontend/e2e/out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local config
#
# Nothing in this section is a substitute for keeping secrets out of the repo in the
# first place. application-local.yml IS committed on purpose — it holds throwaway
# container credentials and no real secret. Production values come from AWS Secrets
# Manager (ADR-010 / DEPLOYMENT.md).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform (Phase 7)
#
# State is remote (S3, S3-native locking — ADR-023), but a stray local state file would
# contain resource IDs and, for some resources, secrets in plaintext. Ignored defensively.
#
# .terraform.lock.hcl is NOT ignored: it pins provider versions and checksums, so every init
# installs the provider that was reviewed — the job gradle-wrapper validation does for Gradle.
# (Ignored here from Phase 0 until 7.2.)
# *.tfvars hold per-person values (alert emails, an allowlisted IP); the .example is committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log
crash.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.log
CLAUDE.md
docs/CLAUDE_MASTER_PROMPT.md
# k6 run output (Phase 8.3+); results worth keeping are summarised in docs/perf/
loadtest/results/
__pycache__/
